Runtime state lives here: api_token (0600) and settings.json. Both are
gitignored; this file exists only so the directory itself is in the repo.

Why that matters: docker-compose bind-mounts ./data, and Docker creates a
missing bind-mount source as root. The container runs as the host user, so it
then cannot write here -- and it does not fail loudly. The backend prints
"Could not save the API token", the token changes on every restart, and
PUT /api/settings answers 200 while the save silently fails.

If you hit that anyway (an older clone, or the directory got recreated):

    sudo chown -R "$(id -u):$(id -g)" data

.dockerignore excludes this directory from the build context, so the token and
your API keys never bake into an image layer.
